      "heading": "B — Audience",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, Section Twelve Sharing the road\n\nThe audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Twelve teaches how to drive around every other road user from pedestrians to heavy trucks. It depends on the definitions chapter for school bus, right-of-way and following distance and on the turning chapter for the three-to-four second rule. The rules progress from pedestrians and school buses, through night driving and motorcycles, to trucks, animals, bicycles and other vulnerable road users.\n",
